# Formats and lints what is staged, then type-checks the project.
#
# `lint-staged` runs eslint --fix and prettier --write over the staged files and
# restages what it rewrites, so a commit lands formatted rather than failing and
# making you do it. Anything eslint cannot fix on its own still fails the commit.
#
# The type-check is whole-project rather than per-file, because a type error is
# rarely in the file that caused it - changing a shared type breaks its callers,
# and those are exactly the files not in this commit. It costs about two seconds.
#
# The Playwright suite is deliberately not here. It needs a production build and
# takes the better part of a minute, which is too much to pay per commit; CI runs
# it on every push and every PR.
npx lint-staged
npm run typecheck
